{# ABOUTME: The OPE v0.2 feed namespace document, served at the namespace URI https://feedspec.org/ope/ns/0.2. #}
{# ABOUTME: Lists the elements and examples from the specification's Feeds profile; the specification is authoritative. #}

<!-- Namespace Header -->
<section class="py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-400/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-emerald-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-emerald-400/20">XML Namespace · OPE v0.2</span>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">OPE Namespace 0.2</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed max-w-lg">This is the namespace URI for the Open Portable Entitlement (OPE) v0.2 feed extensions. RSS and Atom feeds use it to say what is for sale and which items are gated; JSON Feed uses the equivalent <code>_ope</code> extension.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 bg-zinc-900 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-white/10"></span>
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-white/10"></span>
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-white/10"></span>
        <span class="ml-2 text-zinc-400 text-xs">Namespace Declaration</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="p-5 overflow-x-auto m-0 text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed"><span class="text-sky-300">xmlns:ope</span>=<span class="text-amber-300">"https://feedspec.org/ope/ns/0.2"</span></pre>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">The <a href="{{ '/ope/spec/' | url }}#a-feeds-profile" class="text-emerald-700 underline">Feeds profile</a> of the specification is authoritative; this page summarizes it. v0.1 used a different namespace, <a href="{{ '/ope/ns/1.0/' | url }}" class="text-emerald-700 underline">ns/1.0</a>, which is withdrawn.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="{{ '/ope/spec/' | url }}" class="rounded-full bg-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 hover:bg-emerald-400 no-underline transition-colors">Read the Spec</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/shellen/open-portable-entitlement" class="rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-600 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-900/10 hover:text-zinc-900 hover:ring-zinc-900/20 no-underline transition-colors">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Placement -->
<section class="py-16 border-t border-zinc-900/5">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Placement</h2>
    <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 mb-6">Declare Offers once, or per item</p>
    <ul class="space-y-3 list-none p-0 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong class="text-zinc-900">Channel level.</strong> <code>ope:offer</code> on the RSS <code>&lt;channel&gt;</code> or Atom <code>&lt;feed&gt;</code>, naming a scope such as <code>https://lamplighter.example/issues/</code>. It covers every gated item in that scope: one subscription, declared once.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-zinc-900">Item level.</strong> <code>ope:offer</code> on an <code>&lt;item&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;entry&gt;</code>, naming that item's Asset. It replaces the channel-level Offers for that item, as for a one-off paid episode.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-zinc-900">Gated by the channel.</strong> An item covered by channel-level Offers carries an empty <code>ope:asset</code> naming its Asset. An item with neither element isn't gated by OPE.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">The publisher's resource metadata stays authoritative. Feed Offers let a reader show what's for sale without a request per item. Readers without OPE support ignore these elements and show previews as usual.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Elements Reference -->
<section class="py-16 border-t border-zinc-900/5">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Elements</h2>
    <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 mb-8">OPE namespace elements</p>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:offer</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-2">One Offer for an Asset or, on the channel or feed, for a scope of Assets. Repeat it for each Offer (monthly, annual, student).</p>
        <div class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed"><span class="font-semibold text-zinc-700">Attributes:</span> <code>resource</code> (required): the Asset identifier, or a scope ending in <code>/</code> at channel level. <code>metadata</code> (optional, item level only): the Asset's resource metadata URL, used only if it is on the Asset's own origin. <code>id</code> (optional): the Offer's identifier.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:asset</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-2">Empty element marking a gated item that is covered by the channel-level Offers.</p>
        <div class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed"><span class="font-semibold text-zinc-700">Attributes:</span> <code>resource</code> (required), <code>metadata</code> (optional), as on <code>ope:offer</code>.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:name</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">The Offer's name, shown to the reader. Required.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:payment</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-2">How the Offer is paid for. Required.</p>
        <div class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed"><span class="font-semibold text-zinc-700">Attributes:</span> <code>type</code> (required): <code>subscription</code>, <code>purchase</code>, <code>rental</code>, <code>free</code>, <code>contribution</code>, or <code>institutional</code>. <code>amount</code>, <code>currency</code> (ISO 4217), <code>period</code> (ISO 8601 duration such as <code>P1M</code>): optional.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:purchase-url</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">Where a reader with no access goes to get it. Required unless the payment type is <code>free</code> or <code>institutional</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:terms</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-2">Empty element pointing at the publisher's terms. Required.</p>
        <div class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed"><span class="font-semibold text-zinc-700">Attributes:</span> <code>url</code> (required), <code>sha256</code> and <code>type</code> (optional).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:entitlement-types</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">Optional and informational: which of <code>access</code>, <code>limit</code>, <code>status</code> the Offer results in, space-separated.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1"><code class="text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ope:preview-note</code></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">Optional one line to show readers who don't have access.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">In JSON Feed, the same Offer is a JSON object inside <code>_ope</code>: at the top level for the whole feed, or on an item. The specification gives the exact mapping between the XML and JSON forms.</p>
  </div>
</section>

